WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:04.000
June

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.630
SHOGI HALL

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.130
They're huge!

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.130
Whose shoes are these?

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.220
They're freaking enormous!

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.930
- Kumakura 9th-Dan, right?
- Most likely.

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.140
He's here for the qualifier
for the Kiryuu Championship.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:19.720
Hey, what size is it?

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:21.140
Want to check?

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:22.480
Yeah, yeah!

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:31.490
RUMBLE RUMBLE RUMBLE

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:28.730
Whoa, 29.5 cm! Incredible, almost 30 cm!

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:31.490
That's how he kicked that hole in the inn's wall!

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.070
These are beyond human!

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.240
You can't fit these into a cubbyhole!

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.620
But I was shocked, you know?

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:49.130
For that cool, stone-faced Mr. Kumakura to kick
the wall of an inn after losing a title match...

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:55.010
I never realize he had so much hidden passion
beneath that calm exterior.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:57.890
That makes him so much more cooler!

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:00.600
I'm going to start kicking, too!

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:03.940
Kengo, you the man!

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.690
I bet if I put these on,
I can become stronger!

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.570
I'll get closer to Class A!

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.320
I'm starting to believe that!

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:12.820
You might be right!

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.780
You could get closer!

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:16.990
What do you think?

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:20.240
What do you think, Smith?
You think I can be Class A?

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.330
His feet are huge!

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:22.790
You're unbalanced.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.160
But that's fine!

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.210
Sorry to interrupt
when you're having a good time.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.960
But can I have my shoes back?

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.340
S-Sorry!

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:33.590
I-I'm sorry!

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:41.970
Such a giant. So cool.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.100
Look at that trunk.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:46.350
That's not a professional shogi player's body.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:48.100
Is it true he's a 5th dan in judo?

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:52.110
I heard he was invited to join
a mixed martial arts organization!

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.650
Crap! It's already been 25 minutes?

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.030
Our precious 50 minute lunch break
will be over soon!

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.080
Hurry! Oh, no!

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.990
We've only got time
for the soba shop on the corner!

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.930
Nikaidou Family Special
30-Item Bland, Healthy Matsubana Bento

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:45.930
So we've both cleared our first match, huh?

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:54.020
The Newcomer Tournament
is for players 26 years old and younger.

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:57.030
PLUMP

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.030
MOIST

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:57.030
LUXURIOUS

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.650
CHEW CHEW

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:01.030
Players 5th dan and below can compete.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.240
CHEW CHEW

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:04.780
There are 42 players in the tournament.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.030
CHEW CHEW

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.540
However...

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:08.790
NOM NOM

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:12.460
You're always eating healthy but high-class.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.460
You should either eat or talk.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:21.630
KIRIYAMA

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:21.630
NIKAIDOU

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:22.550
Listen. If we win three more times,
we'll reach the finals.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:25.890
You and I won't face off
at any rank-deciding competitions this year.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:25.890
FINALS

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.310
WIPE
WIPE

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.310
The Legend Begins!!

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:32.310
You need to hang in there, no matter what,
so we can battle each other in an official game!

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.400
"I need to hang in there"?

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.940
It sounds like you're pretty confident
about getting to the finals.

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.280
Where does that confidence come from?

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:43.950
Listen! Whatever you do, make it to the finals!

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:47.450
That's where our legend begins!

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.450
PROJECT X
TOP RUNNER

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:52.960
Meijin Nikaidou's Challenge
~ The Rivals are Best Friends ~

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.960
After I become a Meijin,

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:56.460
I'll get featured on a program like Project X,

00:04:56.630 --> 00:05:00.590
and they'll show
black-and-white freeze frames of that match!

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.130
That's what...

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:03.590
Nikaidou thought...

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:04.970
at the time.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.430
HEARTRENDING
QUIVER
QUIVER

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:09.430
It'll have narration like that!

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:13.980
Hey, you're getting way too deep
into that future outlook of yours.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:15.980
And, are you crying?

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:20.030
The Newcomer Tournament, huh?

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:22.280
That brings back...

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:24.030
a lot of memories.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:24.990
GASP

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:30.870
But kid, you should only indulge in such
idle chatter after you beat this old man today.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.200
Got that?

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.120
SMILE

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:37.130
A pie in the sky is tasty, but it won't fill you up.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:38.630
SMILE

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:44.970
Right! I'm looking forward to our game today.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:47.140
I'm sorry we interrupted your lunch!

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:49.600
What's your problem, Kiriyama?

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:51.430
He got mad at us because of you!

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.390
From the gentle Arimoto 9th-Dan!

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.390
GWARRR

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:58.310
No matter how you look at it,
it's all your fault.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:07.030
Talking loudly about winning a title, becoming
a Meijin, and going on NHK's Top Runner...

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:15.870
Kiriyama, you're always going with that
"Oh, I'm not greedy" air,

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:20.460
acting as if you're watching
with the cool detachment of a spectator,

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.630
but I know what's up!

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:26.300
About this Newcomer King, you're like,

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:29.680
"Well, if I play properly,
I can win it without much hassle."

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:31.220
Am I right?

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:33.220
Excuse me?

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:36.390
Wh-Where is that coming from?

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:38.600
What?

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:42.980
"I don't need to make a fuss about the
Newcomer King because of course I'll win it."

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:44.610
"In fact,

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:49.160
regarding the age restriction,
I'm totally confident,

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:55.370
but if I had to worry about anything,
I think I'm getting closer to 6th dan,

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:58.620
so if I don't win soon,
I may miss my chance.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:01.420
Well, I'll cross that bridge when I come to it.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:05.960
There are plenty of other title championships,
so I could always work hard for those."

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:09.840
That's more or less what you're thinking
deep in your heart, isn't it?

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:13.560
What? Of course I don't think that.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.350
Where do you come up
with these ridiculous ideas?

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:18.810
Sheesh.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.570
I would never...

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:25.940
I would...

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.200
Huh?

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:32.570
Wait.

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:37.750
BLUSH

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:42.670
<i>Kiriyama didn't realize it?
That brat pisses me off.</i>

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:45.500
<i>Geez. That's adorable, though, dammit!</i>

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:49.760
<i>That's what I can't stand about a middle school
child prodigy going professional.</i>

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:53.050
<i>Ticks me off. That idiot!</i>

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:55.760
<i>Look at him blushing, the ninny.</i>

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:57.100
<i>God help me, that's cute.</i>

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.140
Relax, Kiriyama!

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:05.070
No matter how puffed up you get with success,
and pretend to be a fake herbivore shogi player,

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:08.820
I won't abandon you over something like that!

00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:10.700
The reason is...

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:14.160
I'm the only one who understands you.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.410
(RIVALS)
BEST FRIENDS

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:17.410
Because we're best friends!

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:21.960
This is so embarrassing! I'm the worst!

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:25.790
Hey, wait! We're not done talking!

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:28.210
Oh, man.

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:31.170
He's so shaken.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:33.590
A fragile teenager.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:36.890
Just leave him be, Nikaidou.
It's funnier this way.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.180
Kiriyama.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:44.560
Good grief, Kiriyama. You don't have to worry,
since this was always a den for demons.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:50.690
You'll only find the strong-willed here,
as arrogant as a fiery soul.

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:58.700
Word of mouth is steadily driving up sales
of our "Puffy-Puffy Daruma."

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:02.460
They're really starting to take root
as a March Town specialty.

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:05.130
And it's all thanks to you girls.

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:06.460
You've made Grandpa really happy.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:07.460
BOOM

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:10.380
Let's get a specialty
in March Town

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:12.510
And so, would you help me
think of an idea for a new sweet?

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:18.260
This one will be a "summer confection," huh?

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:20.680
Something that looks refreshing,

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.890
and would go well with cold, green tea...

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:24.480
<i>Purr-purr...</i>

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:28.190
<i>Have any dried bonito or dried sardines?
I'd be satisfied with just a little.</i>

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:31.690
<i>Can you please pet me a little?</i>

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:38.200
But when it comes to summer, our go-to
is the waterfront series that uses agar, right?

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:41.200
That's right. It's important
to stick to the basics.

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:46.460
It would be perfect if we could
add just a little novelty to that.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:49.090
SCRIBBLE
SCRIBBLE

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:48.340
Momo, any ideas?

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:53.760
Like, what would be fun
to see floating in the pond?

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:55.760
What do you like?

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:57.260
Let's see...

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.260
A duck?

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:01.720
Ducks, huh?

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:04.100
Nice! That'd be cute!

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:06.600
That's my granddaughter!

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:10.110
Oh, but if customers bought it as a souvenir,

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:13.780
the duck could fall off
while they are walking with it.

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:18.820
Good point. As a gift, that shouldn't happen.

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:21.830
What if we sunk it?

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.200
Inside the block of agar?

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:31.630
All of a sudden, it's become something else.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:35.340
Something... kind of sinister?

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:39.930
Momo, any other ideas?

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:44.640
Like something that splashes into the water.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:44.640
SCRIBBLE
SCRIBBLE

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:46.690
Does that bring anything to mind?

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:49.440
Splashes...

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:51.730
into the water?

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:58.490
A sandal?

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:07.000
<i>I dropped my sandal!</i>

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.000
<i>Don't cry.</i>

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.500
<i>I'll buy you new ones.</i>

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:19.510
(VISUAL IMAGE)

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:15.380
<i>It dropped in there, huh? It's okay, it's okay.</i>

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:22.390
<i>A sandal, she says?</i>

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:25.020
We've got a child prodigy here!

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:28.020
Could this girl be a blessing
from the god of sweets?

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:30.060
My granddaughter is the best!

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:32.650
That sensibility is fresh and then some!

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:34.440
It'll be a hit!

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:36.900
Grandpa...

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:41.660
CRESCENT MOON

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:40.950
Will Crescent Moon be okay?

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:45.450
Honestly, what are we
going to do with you, Grandpa?

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:46.660
Right, Hina?

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:04.350
Hina!

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:07.470
Sorry for the wait. The bath's open.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:17.110
What's wrong?

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:19.110
You seem down.

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:25.450
Oh, no. I'm fine.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:31.830
Well...

00:12:33.380 --> 00:12:34.960
I'll go take a bath.

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:41.720
Then don't forget the fire.

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:44.930
You're the last one, so be sure to put it out.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.510
Right, got it.

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:48.470
Good night.

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:50.230
Good night.

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:59.230
Come to think of it,
she left some food on her plate tonight.

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:06.490
Hina...

00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:09.240
I wonder if something happened at school?

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:36.020
June

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:40.030
Ladybug Bush (Part 1)

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:45.360
EGG SALAD SANDWICH

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:49.240
FUJIMORI BAKERY

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:48.580
Thank you!

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:54.500
It's true.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:55.960
It's really good.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:56.500
Bought some
for lunch, too

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:01.630
<i>The egg salad sandwich from
the Fujimori Bakery on 2nd Street is delicious!</i>

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:02.800
LOVE

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:04.010
<i>They're open from early in the morning,</i>

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:07.140
<i>so if you have a match, you could buy your
breakfast there and eat it on the way.</i>

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:04.880
LOVE

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:06.840
LOVE

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:10.640
<i>I love you, Sis!</i>

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:12.140
<i>Fujimori Bakery?</i>

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:15.730
<i>Rei, the doughnuts there are great!</i>

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:18.400
<i>Try them. You have to try them!</i>

00:14:18.610 --> 00:14:21.480
<i>If you go there in the evening,
you'll get them freshly-fried.</i>

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:26.610
<i>Maybe I should've gotten doughnuts, too.</i>

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:27.990
<i>Like Hina recommended.</i>

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:32.200
<i>Then I could've had them
as a snack during the match.</i>

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:39.750
<i>In today's open tournament,</i>

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:41.960
<i>the amount of time the players have is short.</i>

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:50.220
<i>It starts at 10,
so I can go in 15 minutes before that.</i>

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:53.890
<i>I still have time, so I'll eat out here.</i>

00:14:57.350 --> 00:15:00.610
<i>I've played against today's opponent
a number of times before.</i>

00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:02.650
<i>He's good at playing quick games.</i>

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:06.490
<i>Maybe he'll go with the Fujii System...</i>

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:08.990
COFFEE

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:11.870
<i>In that case, it'll be a fast battle.</i>

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:18.580
<i>That bush...</i>

00:15:20.130 --> 00:15:22.340
<i>That's right. I remember.</i>

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.760
<i>There was one in the yard
of my elementary school.</i>

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:29.760
<i>A ladybug bush.</i>

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:36.770
<i>Out of all the bushes there,</i>

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:41.690
<i>for some reason, ladybugs only laid
their eggs on that bush.</i>

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:04.250
<i>I haven't seen one in a long time.</i>

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.420
<i>It makes me feel nostalgic.</i>

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:15.890
<i>Nostalgic?</i>

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:20.020
<i>No, that's not right.</i>

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:23.860
<i>This is... This feeling is...</i>

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:42.580
Uh-oh! He's looking at us!

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:44.710
- I'm scared!
- Four-eyed robot!

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:46.750
You're the one who threw it!

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:55.550
<i>After I lost my parents and little sister
to a car accident,</i>

00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:59.180
<i>I became part of
a shogi-playing family in Tokyo.</i>

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:05.190
<i>My school in Nagano
was small and I was alone.</i>

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.190
<i>But after coming to Tokyo,</i>

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:14.450
<i>I learned the true meaning
of being alone in my huge new school.</i>

00:17:16.570 --> 00:17:20.700
<i>Still, I'd never had a single friend before,</i>

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:20.700
KIRIYAMA THE SHOGI ROBOT

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:24.080
<i>so that was normal for me.</i>

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:29.460
<i>"It's normal."</i>

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:33.340
<i>That's what I tried to think.</i>

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:38.470
SHOGI HALL

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:40.470
<i>I went as far as to make myself unnoticeable
so the direct attacks on me</i>

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:42.810
<i>from my classmates wouldn't escalate.</i>

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:45.980
<i>I was used to that kind of thing,</i>

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:48.980
<i>so I acted indifferent about it every day.</i>

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:55.990
<i>During recess,
I would pretend to be absorbed in a book.</i>

00:17:56.740 --> 00:17:59.990
<i>And for lunch break,
I would stand out if I stayed in the room.</i>

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:05.290
<i>So I'd hide in the bushes
in a corner of the schoolyard.</i>

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:06.920
Pass me the ball!

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:10.500
<i>Rook to 2-3, promoted.</i>

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:13.260
CHECKMATE IN FIVE MOVES
TIME TRIAL

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:13.260
<i>Same, King.</i>

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:15.510
<i>Bishop to 1-3, promoted.</i>

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:19.260
<i>King to 3-4.</i>

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:24.020
<i>My adoptive mother was kind.</i>

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:26.310
Good morning.

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:27.560
Morning.

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:34.650
<i>She always smiled with a worried expression.</i>

00:18:36.910 --> 00:18:40.660
<i>I did everything I could think of
to please Mother, but...</i>

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:43.040
Wash the rice?

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:48.040
Why don't you have Rei do it?
He's better at it than I am, isn't he?

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.040
Clean the bathtub?

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:53.760
You should make Rei do it.

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:56.550
You're always saying
that he's such a good boy, Mom.

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:02.260
<i>The more I helped around the house...</i>

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:12.230
<i>...the more troubled Mother looked.</i>

00:19:14.230 --> 00:19:16.440
- Let's have a good game.
- Let's have a good game.

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:28.460
<i>Listen, could you quit trying to be
so obvious about scoring points?</i>

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:31.080
<i>She's our mom.</i>

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:37.970
<i>I hate him. He's so creepy.</i>

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:39.590
<i>He's like a robot.</i>

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:47.100
<i>At night, I would get stressed, wondering if
the rest of my life would be like this.</i>

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:49.690
<i>I couldn't even breathe.</i>

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:55.360
<i>And so I tried to become
completely absorbed in shogi,</i>

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:58.110
<i>so I wouldn't have to
think about anything else.</i>

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:00.740
<i>For the longest time,</i>

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:06.240
<i>my days were like bobbing on a sea at night,
with my legs failing to reach the bottom.</i>

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:11.250
<i>All I had that I can cling to...</i>

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:13.960
<i>was this little board.</i>

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:19.920
<i>I would solve every last one
of the composed shogi problems</i>

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:23.470
<i>and read until I broke out into a fever.</i>

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:30.980
<i>Then I moved on
to the untouched shogi game records</i>

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:34.730
<i>in Father's study,
50 years' worth of official matches.</i>

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:40.030
<i>From there, beautifully preserved shogi
game records from the Edo era were stored.</i>

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:43.030
<i>I would study them day and night.</i>

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:48.160
<i>I'd spend all of my days off at the Shogi Hall,</i>

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:55.840
<i>or playing shogi from morning to night
at a shogi dojo Father introduced me to.</i>

00:20:57.500 --> 00:21:00.920
<i>I would play, and play, and play,</i>

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:04.260
<i>and play, and keep playing...</i>

00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:08.770
I lost.

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:17.770
<i>I would play, and play, and play,
and play, and play,</i>

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:22.780
<i>and play, and play, and play, and play and play.</i>

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:32.540
Akari Kawamoto
Dinner
Come over for
dinner tonight.
We're having
hamburger steak.
Akari

00:21:34.830 --> 00:21:38.840
<i>And so, that's how I'm here right now.</i>

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:13.720
Welcome. Oh, doughnuts!

00:23:14.310 --> 00:23:15.730
You bought them for us?

00:23:15.730 --> 00:23:17.390
FUJIMORI BAKERY

00:23:18.020 --> 00:23:21.020
They're still a little warm. Freshly-fried, huh?

00:23:21.020 --> 00:23:22.270
GLEAM
GLEAM

00:23:22.690 --> 00:23:24.730
I wanna eat doughnuts!

00:23:25.940 --> 00:23:28.740
It would be nice to eat them
while they're still warm.

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:31.990
But then we wouldn't have room for dinner.

00:23:34.700 --> 00:23:37.120
Hina isn't home yet.

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:38.250
She's late.

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:41.880
<i>What? Can I partake?</i>

00:23:42.170 --> 00:23:44.170
<i>Is it okay? Can I have some?</i>

00:23:45.010 --> 00:23:46.130
Such long arms!

00:23:49.300 --> 00:23:51.300
There she is now.

00:23:51.720 --> 00:23:52.800
Welcome home!

00:23:57.980 --> 00:24:00.690
I wonder what's wrong. Hina?

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:02.190
That's you, right?

00:24:07.820 --> 00:24:08.820
Hina?

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:18.830
Rei...

00:24:18.960 --> 00:24:20.960
S-Sis...

00:24:23.340 --> 00:24:24.460
Hina!

00:24:26.460 --> 00:24:30.010
Ladybug Bush (Part 1)

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:38.060
Episode 26

00:24:32.550 --> 00:24:38.060
Rei brought over many books
about beautiful Japanese-style sweets.

00:24:38.390 --> 00:24:39.770
I see.

00:24:39.770 --> 00:24:44.770
What I thought was the two-spotted ladybug,
was actually called the Asian ladybeetle.

00:24:45.020 --> 00:24:48.440
The word for "ladybug"
actually has a kanji?

00:24:48.570 --> 00:24:50.030
I didn't know.

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:58.330
ILLUSTRATOR:
KENSHI YONEZU

00:24:50.740 --> 00:24:52.280
Go ahead, Momo!

00:24:52.280 --> 00:24:54.780
Please watch
"March comes in like a lion" again!

00:24:54.780 --> 00:24:58.330
Momo is the world's,
no, the galaxy's best granddaughter!
